{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/airnewsalerts/posts/%EF%B8%8F-fake-video-alertpakistani-propaganda-accounts-are-circulating-a-video-of-defen/1414219000901797/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/airnewsalerts/videos/%EF%B8%8F-fake-video-alertpakistani-propaganda-accounts-are-circulating-a-video-of-defen/1682540789469527/","title":"18K views · 248 reactions | ⚠️ Fake Video Alert!\n\n🚨Pakistani propaganda accounts are circulating a video of Defence Minister Rajnath Singh claiming that he made threatening remarks about the protesting students. \n\n#PIBFactCheck:\n\n❌ The video is #Fake and AI-generated.\n\n✅ Defence Minister \n@rajnathsingh\n did NOT make any such statement regarding the Delhi protest.\n\n🔗 Watch the original, unedited video here:\nhttps://x.com/ANI/status/2079855923913441779?s=20\n\n🔴 Report any suspicious content related to the Government of India to \n@PIBFactCheck\n:\n\n📱 WhatsApp: +91 8799711259\n📧 Email: factcheck@pib.gov.in | All India Radio News","description":"⚠️ Fake Video Alert!\n\n🚨Pakistani propaganda accounts are circulating a video of Defence Minister Rajnath Singh claiming that he made threatening remarks about the protesting students....","language":"en","text":"𝐈𝐧𝐝𝐢𝐚 𝐩𝐢𝐭𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 𝐒𝐚𝐦𝐮𝐝𝐫𝐚 𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐭𝐡𝐚𝐧 𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐥𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧, 𝐬𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐜 𝐩𝐞𝐭𝐫𝐨𝐥𝐞𝐮𝐦 𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐬 𝐭𝐨 𝐠𝐥𝐨𝐛𝐚𝐥 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐬 𝐢𝐧 𝐀𝐛𝐮 𝐃𝐡𝐚𝐛𝐢\nOn the sidelines of ADIPEC 2026, India showcased investment and partnership opportunities in its energy sector, hosting two dedicated events in Abu Dhabi that aim to attract global players and strengthen international collaboration in the sector.\nThe Indian Strategic Petroleum Reserves Limited (ISPRL) presented public-private partnership opportunities in India's strategic petroleum reserves programme, highlighting the commercial utilisation of existing storage infrastructure at Visakhapatnam and the proposed development of a 4-million-tonne storage facility at Chandikhol in Odisha.\nIn another event hosted by the Directorate General of Hydrocarbons, India presented opportunities in its upstream exploration sector, with a particular focus on the Samudra Manthan initiative, alongside the upcoming OALP X and XI bidding rounds, sectoral reforms and partnerships with Indian national oil companies.\nSamudra Manthan is an approximately 8.8-billion-dollar programme aimed at accelerating exploration in India's deep and ultra-deepwater basins, with an objective to the country's oil reserves over the next decade.\nDr. Ranjit Rath, CMD, Oil India Limited, said the Samudra Manthan initiative has generated encouraging interest, with India seeking partnerships with global oil companies not just for investment but also for technology, expertise and collaboration to expand its deep and ultra-deepwater exploration activities.\nAmbassador Deepak Mittal highlighted the positive response to both side events, underlining opportunities for international participation in India's strategic petroleum storage projects at Chandikhol and Visakhapatnam.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2082.565763000275,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}